      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "KEY FEATURES\r\n•\tTwo-bedroom semi-detached bungalow\r\n•\tRecently refurbished and presented in excellent condition\r\n•\tNewly fitted contemporary kitchen\r\n•\tNewly upgraded bathroom\r\n•\tNew central heating boiler\r\n•\tBright rear sunroom\r\n•\tLandscaped back garden\r\n•\tQuiet and private cul-de-sac setting\r\n•\tOff-street parking\r\n•\tConvenient location close to town centre\r\n•\tGenerous attic space\r\n•\tRoof design offering excellent attic conversion potential\r\n•\tSimilar attic conversions already undertaken in neighbouring properties\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION\r\nTucked away in a quiet and private cul-de-sac close to the town centre, this recently refurbished two-bedroom semi-detached bungalow combines well-proportioned accommodation with a landscaped back garden, off-street parking and excellent potential to create additional living space.\r\nThe property has recently benefitted from a series of significant improvements and upgrades, including the installation of a new contemporary kitchen, a newly refurbished bathroom and a new central heating boiler.\r\n\r\nAccommodation is arranged entirely at ground floor level and includes two bedrooms together with the principal living areas. To the rear, a bright sunroom overlooks and provides direct access to the landscaped back garden, adding valuable additional living space to the property.\r\nA particularly noteworthy feature of Number 317 is its roof design, which provides a generous attic area with excellent potential for conversion, subject to the necessary planning and building regulations. The possibilities offered by this additional space are demonstrated by neighbouring properties where similar attic conversions have already been completed.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property benefits from its own landscaped back garden, while off-street parking is provided to the front.\r\nRecently refurbished and enhanced by its quiet cul-de-sac position, Number 317 is a well-presented bungalow with the additional benefit of significant potential to increase its existing accommodation.\r\nCall us today to arrange a viewing of this must-see property.\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\nRedford Park is a mature and well-established residential development enjoying a convenient setting within easy reach of Greystones town centre.\r\nGreystones’ enduring appeal has earned international recognition, with the town twice winning Gold at the prestigious International Awards for Liveable Communities (LivCom), first in 2008 and again in 2021, when it was named the World’s Most Liveable Community.\r\nGreystones town centre offers an excellent selection of supermarkets, independent shops, boutiques and other retail outlets, together with the cafés, pubs, bistros and restaurants that have helped establish the town as one of North Wicklow’s most sought-after locations.\r\nThe town is particularly well served by recreational and sporting amenities, including Greystones Marina, the Shoreline Leisure Centre, popular beaches and seafront, along with clubs catering for rugby, GAA, soccer, tennis, golf, sailing, rowing and a wide variety of other sports.\r\nThere is an excellent choice of schools throughout Greystones and neighbouring Delgany, including primary and secondary options, together with a good selection of pre-school and Montessori facilities.\r\n\r\nTransport connections are also excellent. Greystones DART station provides regular services to Dublin, while the town is served by a number of bus routes. The N11 is within easy reach, providing convenient road access to Dublin, the M50 and destinations throughout Wicklow and beyond.\r\nCombining an established coastal town setting with excellent schools, transport connections and an extensive range of shops, services and amenities, Greystones continues to be one of North Wicklow’s most popular residential locations."
      },
